<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Sallie Mae.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Sallie Mae.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Lehman said the absence of the fee on loans will add about $0.50 a share to Student Loan Marketing Association's annual earnings.</p>
<p>-- Lehman said a U.S. court acted earlier than expected when it struck down on Friday a 1991 decision that applies a 30 basis point fee to any loan in which Sallie Mae holds an interest.</p>
<p>-- Uncertainty, however, remains since the case has been remanded back to the U.S. Department of Education.</p>
<p>-- Lehman set a target price of $115 per share.</p>
<p>-- Additional details were not immediately available.</p>
<p>-- Sallie Mae gained 2-5/8 to 94-1/2 on Monday.</p>
<p>(( -- Wall Street desk 212-859-1730))</p>
</text>
